> nothing but "SCSI Bus Reset" errors. Something to do with
> multi-hose machines? Or maybe the bridge chip on the dual-chip
> sym(4) cards? Or a combination of both ;) ?

Hose numbers get lost behind bridges :(
You need to have all bridged cards at the same hose, or maybe even
hose 0.

> A machine with an isp(4) driven card froze during sysinstall
> with a weird usb error. 

I'm not surprised with this if you have an usb controller on another
hose.

> I can dig up the log of that stuff, for now I'm wondering if
> others have seen this too

I've seen something similar on rawhide with multiple bridged cards.
Another issue might be interrupt routing, but I think that's not a
problem on ES40.

